  "own_original_text": "Executive Order 12390 of October 25, 1982\nDelegation to the Secretary of State\nBy the authority vested in me as President of the United States of America by  \nSection 301 of Title 3 of the United States Code, in order to assign certain  \nfunctions to the Secretary of State, it is hereby ordered as follows:\nSection 1. The functions vested in the President by Section 306 of the  \nSupplemental Appropriations Act of 1982 (Public Law 97-257) are delegated to  \nthe Secretary of State.\nSec. 2. Before making the determination and providing the written reports  \nreferred to in that Section 306, the Secretary of State shall confer with the  \nSecretary of the Treasury and, as appropriate, with the Secretary of Agricul­\nture and the heads of other interested Executive agencies.\nSec. 3. Similar functions vested in the President by Section 205 of Public Law  \n97-216 were delegated to the Secretary of State. The performance by the  \nSecretary of State of those functions is confirmed and ratified.\nTHE WHITE HOUSE,  \nO ctober 25, 1982.\n[FR Doc. 82-29799 \nFiled 10-26-82; 2:28 pm]",
